1. A program for executing a quest using a deck organized from a number of owned contents not exceeding a predetermined number among contents owned by a player,
the program causing a computer to function as:
a storage means for storing, in association with the quest, a clear deck which is a deck used when the quest has been cleared;
a determination means for determining, when the player has failed to clear the quest, whether a clear deck associated with the quest can be organized from the contents owned by the player;
a specifying means for specifying, when the determination is negative, as specific contents, contents that are lacking from the clear deck among the contents owned by the player; and
a control means for displaying to the player an acquisition screen for obtaining the specific contents by consuming a cost.

2. A program for executing a quest using a deck organized from a number of owned contents not exceeding a predetermined number among contents owned by a player,
the program causing a computer to function as:
a storage means for storing, in association with the quest, a clear deck which is a deck used when the quest has been cleared;
a determination means for determining, when the player selects a quest to execute, whether a clear deck associated with the quest can be organized from the contents owned by the player;
a specifying means for specifying, when the determination is negative, as specific contents, contents that are lacking from the clear deck among the contents owned by the player; and
a control means for displaying, before the player executes the selected quest, an acquisition screen for obtaining the specific contents by consuming a cost.
